20,299,155 eligible public parent rows finds no competing eligible row within $1\arcsec$ of either
the cluster or canonical-original-member coordinate for any released candidate.  One case,
\texttt{P3-DESI-000039}, has a second warning-free primary eligible row at $1.0498\arcsec$ from
both centers, hence within $2\arcsec$ but outside the declared radius; the released row is at
$0.2213\arcsec$.  The machine-readable audit publishes every row found within both radii.

\subsection{Deterministic local-shift association control}\label{sec:chance-control}

Catalog-key uniqueness does not estimate false association.  We therefore repeated the spherical
join after shifting every one of the 190,015 cluster positions along great circles by 60 and
120$\arcsec$ at each of eight fixed position angles.  These 16 realizations retain the local sky
density and footprint on arcminute scales while moving well beyond the declared radius.  The
28,425,963-row FITS table was streamed once against the observed and shifted trees.  For each
realization we retained the nearest eligible target to each shifted cluster and counted associated
cluster positions over the fixed radius grid shown in Figure~\ref{fig:chance-control}.

For the 20,299,155-row science-bit parent, 2,468 observed cluster positions have an association
within $1\arcsec$, versus a shifted mean of 86.69 (sample standard deviation 14.42; range 66--109).
At $0.1\arcsec$, the comparison is 2,456 observed versus a shifted mean of 0.75.  Applying the
global-primary and \texttt{ZWARN}=0 predicates to the background targets gives 181 observed versus
76.19 (13.30; 61--103) within $1\arcsec$, and 170 observed versus 0.625 within $0.1\arcsec$.
The observed strict $0.1$--$1\arcsec$ annulus contains 11 rows, whereas the shifted annulus mean
is 75.56 (13.01; 61--101).  Thus the sub-$0.1\arcsec$ core has strong aggregate association
evidence, but the 11-row tail does not acquire secure candidate-level identity from positional
coincidence alone.  We retain and flag it for auditability rather than subtracting an estimated
background or claiming a corrected purity.  The shifts are correlated local controls, not an
independent Poisson experiment or a selection-function model.

