Their respective interquartile ranges are [0.61636, 1.40103] versus [0.40655, 1.31527] in
$z$; [5.15557, 5.64065] versus [5.35522, 6.66982] in historical score;
[0.000833, 0.001668] versus [0.000926, 0.001685]$\arcsec$ in separation; and
[30.9988, 235.084] versus [1.77359, 17.3439] in \texttt{DELTACHI2}.  The warned table contains
2,194 GALAXY, 72 QSO, and one STAR rows, while the accepted table contains 157, 23, and one.
These contrasts show that the gate is associated most directly with fit discrimination and also
changes the score/redshift composition.  They do not estimate selection probabilities, correct
bias, or promote warning-bearing rows into the primary catalog.

